<article class="env-definition" id="09FR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09FR">Definition <span data-tag="09FR">9.5.1</span>.</a> The <em>characteristic</em> of a field $F$ is $0$ if $\mathbf{Z} \subset F$, or is a prime $p$ if $p = 0$ in $F$. The <em>prime subfield of $F$</em> is the smallest subfield of $F$ which is either $\mathbf{Q} \subset F$ if the characteristic is zero, or $\mathbf{F}_ p \subset F$ if the characteristic is $p > 0$. </p>
</article>